 "title": "Ms 1582, f. 2r, cipher lines 5 to 9",
 "caption": "Five lines of the recto as transcribed, each sign with the value the re-derived key gives it, applied mechanically: “… [a]vons souvent comporté et dissimulé beaucop de choses aux françois et que ceste dernière rompture ilz l’ont faicte comme tout le monde scait voluntairement et par leur libre election sans cause quelconque que tou[tesfois] …”. The slips are the key’s: the sign labelled w, for one, is a in some places and l in others. A sign the two transcriptions name differently is marked. The sign names are the transcribers’ labels for shapes, not the shapes themselves. Bibliothèque municipale de Besançon, Ms 1582, f. 2r (no image is shown).",
 "unit": "signs",
